{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1413339-deadliest-monsters-you-can-make","id":1413339,"title":"Deadliest Monsters you can make?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-13T00:30:47-07:00","id":1413339,"title":"Deadliest Monsters you can make?","content":"Recently I have been inspired playing Dwarf Fortress on how in particular Necromancers since the new update for the game can make various unique creatures that aren't undead and appoint them into their armies or just sic them in the wilds for whatever reason. Without the use of Arch-Spheres (because getting to that ranking is extremely hard XP and roleplay wise), what are some of the deadliest Monsters a Mage can make?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T02:52:32-07:00","id":1413354,"title":"","content":"Use imagination. I can think about mythic beasts, powerful spirits and hybrids<br /> <br /> Monsters in other gamelines also work<br /> For example I think battle ghoul Vozhd can be made by Mind 5, Life 5 and Matter 3+<br /> If Arch-spheres is not a thing. You can create Perfect M\u00e9tis (he is a monster), or any flawless supernatural <br /> <br /> IIRC the successes you make on the create roll is distributed on monsters\u2019 Traits , so in theory you can make something without limitation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T03:03:04-07:00","id":1413355,"title":"","content":"NT-1s maybe, they're like T1000 Terminators<br /> <br /> maybe they could combine it with another HIT mark to make a Rev-9","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T17:11:32-07:00","id":1413461,"title":"","content":"Depending on the sphere's you use, you can technically make anything(with enough successes). Making a spirit Incarna would &quot;just&quot; be Spirit 5 + Prime 3, but it'd require more quintessence and successes on the ritual roll than anyone could reasonably produce in our lifetime.<br /> <br /> Just remember that creating something whole cloth(creating a new organism, creating a mind, creating a soul, etc.) is always a sphere 5 effect. You could make changes to an existing thing/creature with spheres at 3, but making those changes permanent will require prime 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 09-13-2020, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-13T20:17:41-07:00","id":1413483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1413339-deadliest-monsters-you-can-make?p=1413461#post1413461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making a spirit Incarna would &amp;quot;just&amp;quot; be Spirit 5 + Prime 3, but it'd require more quintessence and successes on the ritual roll than anyone could reasonably produce in our lifetime.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Difficulty and successes you need will be big as hell<br /> <br /> Although IN THEORY you can create one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T20:59:20-07:00","id":1413702,"title":"","content":"If you don't care about the life of the thing you're enhancing, charms/gadgets can provide a very cheap and simple way to make horrible paradox dumpsterfire monsters. Someone with Life 3 Prime 3 can give one of their minions a bunch of 'upgrade' charms that last about a day and boost a physical stat by 1. Paradox and the user's willpower is really the only limiter. If they had life 4, they could make stronger charms that can be applied by the creator in their sanctum, then the only consequences will be on the victim through Disbelief.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26088-actual_table","name":"Actual_Table","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26088_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T21:08:23-07:00","id":1413703,"title":"","content":"What about reality zones? What if you specifically make an entity that is an analogue to a notorious cryptid/urban legend to the region your in, would Disbelief effect the creature you made?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-14T22:08:22-07:00","id":1413710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1413339-deadliest-monsters-you-can-make?p=1413703#post1413703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about reality zones? What if you specifically make an entity that is an analogue to a notorious cryptid/urban legend to the region your in, would Disbelief effect the creature you made?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would probably be fine, until it wanders out of it's appropriate reality zone. Legends and myths are super useful for making scary monsters though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26088-actual_table","name":"Actual_Table","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26088_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T05:06:39-07:00","id":1413754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1413339-deadliest-monsters-you-can-make?p=1413461#post1413461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depending on the sphere's you use, you can technically make anything(with enough successes). Making a spirit Incarna would &amp;quot;just&amp;quot; be Spirit 5 + Prime 3, but it'd require more quintessence and successes on the ritual roll than anyone could reasonably produce in our lifetime.<br /> <br /> Just remember that creating something whole cloth(creating a new organism, creating a mind, creating a soul, etc.) is always a sphere 5 effect. You could make changes to an existing thing/creature with spheres at 3, but making those changes permanent will require prime 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>No? Creating new objects is Prime 2, Matter 2.","signat